% Exit status of abc2midi -BF (Barfly stress model) when no stress model
% applies.  Tune 1 is a rhythm/meter pair with no built-in model ("Polka" in
% 2/2, as reported in EasyABC ticket #81); tune 2 has no R: field at all.
% Both are valid abc: abc2midi renders them without stress and reports a
% warning, so the exit status is 0.  It used to report an error, and since
% abc2midi started returning 1 on errors, EasyABC refused to play such tunes
% whenever its Barfly option was enabled.  With -Werror the warning becomes
% an error again and the exit status is 1.
X:1
T:Polka in 2/2
C:abc2midi test
R:Polka
M:2/2
L:1/8
K:G
GABc d2B2|c2A2 B2G2|

X:2
T:No rhythm
C:abc2midi test
M:6/8
L:1/8
K:ADor
EAA A2B|cBA BAG|
